  <h2>What size is an Instagram Reel cover?</h2>

  <p>Instagram's Help Center and its developer reference don't agree on the shape.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">The recommended size for cover photos is 420 by 654 pixels (1:1.55), and a cover can't be edited after it is uploaded. Through the API, a cover is a JPEG up to 8MB; a non-9:16 image is cropped to its middle 9:16 rectangle, and to its middle square for a Reel shared to feed.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Instagram Help Center, "Reel size &amp; aspect ratios on Instagram," and Instagram developer reference, "IG User Media," read October 8, 2026. https://help.instagram.com/1038071743007909</p>

  <p>The cover is also the one thing you can't fix later. Build it as a 9:16 frame and keep the face or the product in the middle third (vertically and horizontally). That way it survives both crops the developer reference describes, the 9:16 rectangle and the feed's center square.</p>

