  <h2>How do you publish a Reel or a Story from hubStudio?</h2>

  <p>In the hubStudio app, Instagram in the menu holds every post. Connect an Instagram professional account, Business or Creator, on My Connections first. Then pick the shape: One image, Carousel or Reel. Render the clip with AI, pick it from the Assets Library, or upload it.</p>

  <p>The pencil on the clip opens it in the Video editor, on its Social panel, set to an Instagram Reel at 9:16 and 1080 by 1920. Story, Feed portrait and Square are the other placements, and Crop to fill or Fit it whole decides how every clip takes the shape.</p>

  <p>Leave Show what the network covers on. It draws, in red, where Instagram's name, caption, reply box and buttons sit, with a dashed line around the safe area and another for the profile grid crop. The Checks flag text under those zones, a length the placement won't take or a file that's too heavy, and most of them carry a fix button, such as Move the captions into the safe area.</p>

  <p>The Cover panel picks the frame shown before the video plays and saves it as a JPG, ready for Instagram's own cover picker. Save and use it in the post swaps the edit in as a new version; the original stays in the Assets Library. Editing is free. Only the editor's fast captions are billed from your prepaid balance, at the price shown before you start.</p>

  <p>On the publishing step, a picture goes out as a Feed post or a Story. A video always goes out as a Reel, from 3 seconds to 15 minutes. Publish now or schedule it (one post can go to up to 20 accounts), and publishing to Instagram through hubStudio costs nothing. <a href="/app/publish">The app's publishing page</a> covers every network the app posts to.</p>

  <p>Would you rather a studio cut the Reels? The <a href="/services/design/short-video">short video design service</a> and the <a href="/solutions/platforms/meta">Meta platform page</a> describe how our team produces for Meta's apps.</p>

  <h2>What is the China counterpart to Reels?</h2>

  <p>Douyin runs on the same vertical frame, but its creator surfaces serve no spec text to a reader who isn't logged in. Our <a href="/resources/insights/douyin-video-specs-safe-zones">Douyin video specs and safe zones</a> guide publishes the figure most sources agree on, with the count and a disclaimer. Read it before the same 9:16 master goes to China.</p>

